  "goodToKnow": "Der Storch is a stork; in German folklore, der Klapperstorch brings babies, and children were told so for generations. White storks nest on roofs and church towers, and the village of Rühstädt in Brandenburg calls itself Europe's stork village. Most German storks migrate to Africa in August and return in spring, though more now winter in Spain. Wie der Storch im Salat means walking stiffly. Plural: die Störche."
